{"count":1106,"next":"https://api.afp.mil.ph/articles/?page=7&page_size=100","previous":"https://api.afp.mil.ph/articles/?page=5&page_size=100","results":[{"id":695,"title":"Philippine Navy hosts Exercise SAMASAMA","slug":"philippine-navy-hosts-exercise-samasama","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/277351763_332811928881224_7440173074601394112_n.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"850\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/277351763_332811928881224_7440173074601394112_n.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Philippine Navy is set to host this year’s iteration of the PH-US Exercise SAMASAMA that is scheduled from 02 to 13 October 2023 at the Naval Forces Southern Luzon (NFSL) Area of Operations. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">SAMASAMA is a bilateral exercise between the United States Navy (USN) and the Philippine Navy (PN) that aims to further strengthen international defense cooperation and advance a rules-based international order.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/277351763_332811928881224_7440173074601394112_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-27T00:08:50+08:00","hits":2448},{"id":696,"title":"AFP Chief to PH Navy: fight for our sovereign rights and territorial integrity","slug":"afp-chief-to-ph-navy-fight-for-our-sovereign-rights-and-territorial-integrity","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/PN2.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/PN2.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>The Chief of Staff, AFP, General Romeo S Brawner PA greets the Philippine Navy troops during his Official Visit to their Headquarters on September 26. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Navy personnel were reminded by the Armed Forces Chief today to fight for the nation’s sovereign rights and territory during his visit at the Navy Headquarters this morning. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“Let us always bear in mind our own interests. We are Filipinos, and we will fight for the Philippines’ rights, our sovereign rights, and our territorial integrity,” General Romeo S Brawner Jr, the Armed Forces of the Philippines Chief of Staff said. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/PN2.jpg","image_caption":"The Chief of Staff, AFP, General Romeo S Brawner PA greets the Philippine Navy troops during his Official Visit to their Headquarters on September 26. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-26T08:50:18+08:00","hits":1084},{"id":697,"title":"CSAFP lauds PAF’s support to ground troops, ops","slug":"csafp-lauds-paf-s-support-to-ground-troops-ops","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/PAF4.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/PAF4.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>General Romeo Brawner Jr, the CSAFP, poses for a photo with the officers, enlisted personnel, and civilian employees of the Philippine Air Force at the Villamor Air Base during his official visit and talk to troops on September 25. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAO, AFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, lauded the Philippine Air Force for its dedication towards serving the country as he thanked its pilots and crew who have supported ground troops in its operations over the years.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The CSAFP gave this message to the officers, enlisted personnel, and civilian employees in Villamor Air Base during his visit and talk to troops on September 25.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/PAF4.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, the CSAFP, poses for a photo with the officers, enlisted personnel, and civilian employees of the Philippine Air Force at the Villamor Air Base during his official visit and talk to troops on September 25. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAO, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-25T06:26:57+08:00","hits":852},{"id":698,"title":"Tourists flock to 6ID’s ‘Symbol of Peace’","slug":"tourists-flock-to-6id-s-symbol-of-peace","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/pea.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/pea.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>MGen Alex Rillera, 6ID Commander, poses for a photo with visitors of the Symbol of Peace in Camp Siongco, Datu Odin Sinsuat, Maguindanao Del Norte.</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Symbol of Peace inaugurated on Thursday, September 21, is now attracting tourists and raising awareness on the government’s whole-of-nation efforts to end all armed conflict.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The monument is an eighteen-foot replica of an M-16 crafted from dismantled firearms that were confiscated, captured, recovered or were surrendered to the military as part of its efforts to end violence and proliferation of illegal firearms in the Bangsamoro region.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/pea.jpg","image_caption":"MGen Alex Rillera, 6ID Commander, poses for a photo with visitors of the Symbol of Peace in Camp Siongco, Datu Odin Sinsuat, Maguindanao Del Norte.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-22T06:02:48+08:00","hits":857},{"id":699,"title":"PH, Canadian Navy sail together in WPS","slug":"ph-canadian-navy-sail-together-in-wps","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/SAIL1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"638\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/SAIL1.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>Philippine Navy's BRP Antonio Luna (FF151) and the Canadian Navy's HMCS Ottawa during their joint sail on September 21 in the West Philippine Sea. (Photo from WESCOM)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--More nations are sailing with the Philippines as the Philippine Navy guided-missile frigate BRP Antonio Luna (FF151) completed a bilateral sail in the West Philippine Sea on September 21 this time with the Canadian Halifax-class frigate HMCS Ottawa (FFH341).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Starting at around 7:23 in the morning, the two ships met and established radio communications in the vicinity of Malampaya Natural Gas Platform and performed maneuvers for Officers of the Watch (OOWs) that lasted until around 10 o'clock. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/SAIL1.jpg","image_caption":"Philippine Navy's BRP Antonio Luna (FF151) and the Canadian Navy's HMCS Ottawa during their joint sail on September 21 in the West Philippine Sea. (Photo from WESCOM)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-22T05:56:16+08:00","hits":936},{"id":700,"title":"INTERNATIONAL DAY OF PEACE","slug":"international-day-of-peace","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/IDP1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/IDP1.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>In celebration of the International Day of Peace, personnel from the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) joined the Peace One Day Forum 2023 initiated by the Rotary International District 3830 on September 21 at the Asia Pacific College, Makati City. (Photo by PO3 Viluan Ret/PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Coinciding with the International Day of Peace, the role of the men and women in uniform in peacebuilding was recognized by the Rotary International District 3830 during the Peace One Day Forum 2023 on September 21 at the Asia Pacific College, Makati City.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines joined the Rotary-initiated forum which focused on the Quest for a Hopeful and Peaceful World and provided an in-depth understanding of the country's current peace and security landscape. It also serves as a call to action for law enforcement bodies and the community to collectively work together in promoting peace amidst challenges./// (Photo by PO3 Viluan Ret/PAOAFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/IDP1.jpg","image_caption":"In celebration of the International Day of Peace, personnel from the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) joined the Peace One Day Forum 2023 initiated by the Rotary International District 3830 on September 21 at the Asia Pacific College, Makati City. (Photo by PO3 Viluan Ret/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-21T08:14:00+08:00","hits":494},{"id":701,"title":"CSAFP calls for talks to end divide","slug":"csafp-calls-for-talks-to-end-divide","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/DIV2.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/DIV2.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>General Romeo Brawner Jr with OPAPRU Secretary Carlito Garlvez Jr and other guests lead the unveiling of the Symbol of Peace on September 21 at the headquarters of 6th Infantry Division in Maguindanao del Norte. (Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAO, AFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), called for ‘meaningful conversations’ to end conflict and foster understanding during the unveiling and blessing of the Symbol of Peace on September 21 at the headquarters of 6th Infantry Division in Maguindanao del Norte.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The monument is an eighteen-foot replica of an M-16 crafted from dismantled firearms that were confiscated, captured, recovered or were surrendered to the military as part of its efforts to end violence and proliferation of illegal firearms in the Bangsamoro region.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/DIV2.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr with OPAPRU Secretary Carlito Garlvez Jr and other guests lead the unveiling of the Symbol of Peace on September 21 at the headquarters of 6th Infantry Division in Maguindanao del Norte. (Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAO, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-21T04:24:48+08:00","hits":635},{"id":702,"title":"Philippine Navy flagship interacts with Royal Canadian Navy counterparts departing from their recent goodwill visit","slug":"philippine-navy-flagship-interacts-with-royal-canadian-navy-counterparts-departing-from-their-recent-goodwill-visit","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/CAN1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"847\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/CAN1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">BRP JOSE RIZAL (FF150), HMCS OTTAWA, NRU ASTERIX, and CESSNA 353 from Naval Air Wing - Philippine Fleet carried out series of drills on September 19, 2023. They practiced various maneuvers, including DIVTACS, Replenishment at Sea (RAS) Approaches, and Photo exercises. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The interaction was highlighted by a  Passing Exercise to bid farewell to the visiting vessels. The Philippine Navy extends this custom to all foreign navies during their goodwill visit as a gesture of courtesy and respect.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">(Story and Photo by:  BRP Jose Rizal FF150 - PF)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/CAN1.jpg","image_caption":"Philippine Navy flagship interacts with Royal Canadian Navy counterparts departing from their recent goodwill visit on September 18.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-21T02:43:33+08:00","hits":368},{"id":703,"title":"123 would-be trafficking-in-persons rescued in successful support to law enforcement ops in Sulu","slug":"123-would-be-trafficking-in-persons-rescued-in-successful-support-to-law-enforcement-ops-in-sulu","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/ht1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"1133\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/ht1.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>The Naval Forces Western Mindanao, thru its Naval Task Force 61 together with other law enforcement agencies, successfully rescued would-be trafficking-in-persons in Brgy. Aluh Bunah, Pangutaran, Sulu on September 19, 2023.</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">On September 19, 2023, Naval Forces Western Mindanao (NFWM) and other law enforcement organizations successfully rescued 123 people from becoming victims of human trafficking on Tubalubac Island in Pangutaran, Sulu. Additionally, the operation resulted in the recovery of war materials and illegal drugs<br /><br />The rescued trafficking victims were handed over to Ministry of Social Services and Development-BARMM (MSSD-BARMM) for documentation and assistance. The seized evidence was taken to CIDG Sulu-PFU for documentation and proper handling. Reports reveal that most of the rescued victims were from Cebu and Bohol, and they were forced to do difficult labor in spearfishing while being compelled to consume illegal drugs, specifically shabu, to cope with their difficult work conditions.<br /><br />(Story and Photo by: <span class=\"xv78j7m\" spellcheck=\"false\">Naval Forces Western Mindanao</span>)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/ht1.jpg","image_caption":"The Naval Forces Western Mindanao, thru its Naval Task Force 61 together with other law enforcement agencies, successfully rescued would-be trafficking-in-persons in Brgy. Aluh Bunah, Pangutaran, Sulu on September 19, 2023.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-21T01:10:52+08:00","hits":417},{"id":704,"title":"AFP, Bangladesh mulls defense cooperation through training and education","slug":"afp-bangladesh-mulls-defense-cooperation-through-training-and-education","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/BAN5.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/BAN5.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>MGen Noel Beleran PN(M), Deputy Chief of Staff for Education, Training and Doctrine, J8 welcomes BGen Kazi Anisuzzaman, Directing Staff Army-6, National Defense College to the General Headquarters on September 20. (Photos by PO3 Viluan Ret/PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — Sharing a similar vision in building good relationships with partner countries, MGen Noel Beleran PN(M), Deputy Chief of Staff for Education, Training and Doctrine, J8 meets with BGen Kazi Anisuzzaman, Directing Staff Army-6, National Defense College, Mirpur Cantonment in a Courtesy Visit here on September 20.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“We are planning to establish our defense cooperation and our shared responsibility through education and training in pursuit of a more stable Indo-Pacific,” said MGen Beleran.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/BAN5.jpg","image_caption":"MGen Noel Beleran PN(M), Deputy Chief of Staff for Education, Training and Doctrine, J8 welcomes BGen Kazi Anisuzzaman, Directing Staff Army-6, National Defense College to the General Headquarters on September 20. (Photos by PO3 Viluan Ret/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-21T00:11:41+08:00","hits":481},{"id":705,"title":"AFP, Aus Defence College share practices in training military leaders","slug":"afp-aus-defence-college-share-practices-in-training-military-leaders","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/ausdc4.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"548\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/ausdc4.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>MGen Noel Beleran PN(M), Deputy Chief of Staff for Education, Training and Doctrine, J8 hands over a token to Wing Commander Nicholas Pausina, Australian Defence College at the General Headquarters on September 19. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — The Deputy Chief of Staff for Education, Training and Doctrine, J8, MGen Noel Beleran PN(M) welcomed the delegates of the Australian Command and Staff College headed by the Australian Defence College, Wing Commander Nicholas Pausina in their Study Visit to the country on September 19 at the AFP Headquarters. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“We are really looking forward to the opportunity to engage today. It is very much about the opportunity to expand our relationship. We are hoping to learn a lot,” said Wing Commander Pausina.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/ausdc4.jpg","image_caption":"MGen Noel Beleran PN(M), Deputy Chief of Staff for Education, Training and Doctrine, J8 hands over a token to Wing Commander Nicholas Pausina, Australian Defence College at the General Headquarters on September 19. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-20T00:37:28+08:00","hits":904},{"id":706,"title":"CHANGE OF CHIEF OF OFFICE CEREMONY | AFP Real Estate Office","slug":"change-of-chief-of-office-ceremony-afp-real-estate-office","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/COCA4.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"617\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/COCA4.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>LtGen Charlton Sean M Gaerlan PN(M), The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP hands over the office symbol to the Incoming Chief, AFPREO, Col Froilando G Angat PAF(GSC) during the Change of Chief of Office Ceremony of the AFP Real Estate Office on September 19 in Camp Aguinaldo. (Photo by Sgt Ambay/PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines Real Estate Office (AFPREO) welcomed its new Chief, Col Froilando G Angat PAF(GSC) replacing Col Arcangel G Gamido PAF(GSC) in a Change of Chief of Office Ceremony conducted with The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP (TDCSAFP), LtGen Charlton Sean M Gaerlan PN(M) as the Presiding Officer on September 19 in Camp Aguinaldo.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">“As the AFP pivots to a modernized Armed Forces, the role of the AFPREO is significant, more so in securing and maintaining the rights of the AFP over its real estate properties all over the country. To the Team AFPREO, the dedication to the service of your office is more significant now than ever. I urge you to give the same amount of enthusiasm and support to your new Chief, keeping in mind that as you fulfill the mandate that is expected of you, you are furthering the AFP’s vision of becoming a world-class Armed Forces that is a source of national pride,” said LtGen Gaerlan.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">AFPREO is one of the Personal Staff of the Chief of Staff, AFP (CSAFP) mandated to assist the CSAFP in the administration and management of the AFP Real Estate and Housing Programs./// <span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Photo by Sgt Ambay/PAOAFP)</span></div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/COCA4.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Charlton Sean M Gaerlan PN(M), The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP hands over the office symbol to the Incoming Chief, AFPREO, Col Froilando G Angat PAF(GSC) during the Change of Chief of Office Ceremony of the AFP Real Estate Office on September 19 in Camp Aguinaldo. (Photo by Sgt Ambay/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-20T00:24:05+08:00","hits":1317},{"id":707,"title":"AFP RECEIVES NEW ISR AIRCRAFT","slug":"afp-receives-new-isr-aircraft","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/ISR.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/ISR.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>Secretary of National Defense, Gilberto Teodoro Jr, leads the formal acceptance, turn-over, and blessing of the the Cessna-208B (C-208B) Grand Caravan EX with the Chief of Staff, AFP, Gen Romeo S Brawner; NOLCOM Commander LtGen Fernyl Buca; Philippine Air Force Commanding General, LtGen Stephen P Parreño; and Chief of Joint U.S. Military Assistance Group (JUSMAG)-Philippines, Col Edward R Evans on September 19 at Clark Air Base, Pampanga. (Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAO, AFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines received a brand-new Cessna-208B (C-208B) Grand Caravan EX Intelligence, Surveillance, and Reconnaissance (ISR) aircraft on September 19 that will boost the AFP’s capability to protect Philippine territory and sovereign rights.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/ISR.jpg","image_caption":"Secretary of National Defense, Gilberto Teodoro Jr, leads the formal acceptance, turn-over, and blessing of the the Cessna-208B (C-208B) Grand Caravan EX with the Chief of Staff, AFP, Gen Romeo S Brawner; NOLCOM Commander LtGen Fernyl Buca; Philippine Air Force Commanding General, LtGen Stephen P Parreño; and Chief of Joint U.S. Military Assistance Group (JUSMAG)-Philippines, Col Edward R Evans on September 19 at Clark Air Base, Pampanga. (Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAO, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-19T08:34:48+08:00","hits":695},{"id":708,"title":"General Brawner thanks AUS Army for training PH troops","slug":"general-brawner-thanks-aus-army-for-training-ph-troops","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/AUS4.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/AUS4.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>Gen Romeo Brawner Jr receives a memento from LtGen Simon Stuart during the latter’s courtesy visit to the AFP General Headquarters on September 18. (Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAO, AFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, expressed his appreciation to the Australian Army during the courtesy visit of Australia’s Army Chief, LtGen Simon Stuart on September 18 at the AFP General Headquarters here.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In their meeting, the two discussed PH-Aus bilateral military partnership, including training, student exchanges, reservist development, non-commissioned officer empowerment, and recruitment. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/AUS4.jpg","image_caption":"Gen Romeo Brawner Jr receives a memento from LtGen Simon Stuart during the latter’s courtesy visit to the AFP General Headquarters on September 18. (Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAO, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-18T07:19:40+08:00","hits":1391},{"id":709,"title":"AFP, USINDOPACOM wrap-up MDB-SEB meeting, underscore joint commitments","slug":"afp-usindopacom-wrap-up-mdb-seb-meeting-underscore-joint-commitments","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/mdbseb.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/mdbseb.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>General Romeo Brawner Jr and Admiral John Aquilino pose for a photo during the MDB-SEB meeting on September 14 at Camp Aguinaldo in Quezon City. (Photo by PO3 VIluan Ret/PAO, AFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the US Indo-Pacific Command (US INDOPACOM) concluded its annual Mutual Defense Board-Security Engagement Board (MDB-SEB) meeting at the AFP General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City on September 14, 2023.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the AFP (CSAFP), and Admiral John Aquilino, Commander of US INDOPACOM) led the event that was marked by fruitful discussions and strategic collaboration reaffirming the steadfast commitment of the PH-US in safeguarding our nations and the Indo-Pacific region. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/mdbseb.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-16T08:50:51+08:00","hits":775},{"id":710,"title":"GOOD DOGS | VISCOM awards Military Working Dog Achievement Medals to Mugie and Puti","slug":"good-dogs-viscom-awards-military-working-dog-achievement-medals-to-mugie-and-puti","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/MP2 1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"585\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/MP2 1.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>VISCOM Commander LtGen Benefict M Arevalo, confers the Military Working Dog Achievement Medal to Mugie for his significant contributions to AFPMS campaign in the region.</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Visayas Command (VISCOM) proudly recognized the exceptional contributions of two remarkable canines, Mugie and Puti, in their relentless support of our campaign in the Visayas region. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In a heartwarming ceremony, VISCOM Commander Lieutenant General Benedict M. Arevalo PA, conferred the  Military Working Dog Achievement Medals upon these two heroic four-legged comrades at 302nd Infantry Brigade, Camp Leon Kilat, Negros Oriental. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/MP1.jpg","image_caption":"VISCOM Commander LtGen Benefict M Arevalo, confers the Military Working Dog Achievement Medal to Puti for his significant contributions to AFPMS campaign in the region.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-14T08:01:04+08:00","hits":917},{"id":711,"title":"CA CONFIRMATION | SND and 11 AFP Senior Officers","slug":"ca-confirmation-snd-and-11-afp-senior-officers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/cac4.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/cac4.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>The Commission on Appointments approved the nomination and appointment of 11 AFP senior officers during a session held in Manila on September 13, 2023. (Photo by SN1 Viluan / PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Commission on Appointments (CA) approved the interim appointments and nomination of Department of National Defense Secretary Gilberto \"Gibo\" C. Teodoro, Jr. and 11 AFP senior officers during a session in Manila on September 13, 2023.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Secretary Teodoro along with other AFP senior officers have exhibited exceptional competence throughout their service which garnered the approval and trust of CA.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Below is the complete list of ad interim appointments and nomination approved by the CA:<br />","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/cac4.jpg","image_caption":"The Commission on Appointments approved the nomination and appointment of 11 AFP senior officers during a session held in Manila on September 13, 2023. (Photo by SN1 Viluan / PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-14T07:38:27+08:00","hits":1352},{"id":712,"title":"PH-US pleased with pace of EDCA projects","slug":"ph-us-pleased-with-pace-of-edca-projects","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/MDB2.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/MDB2.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>General Romeo Brawner Jr, Admiral John Aquilino, and US Ambassador MaryKay Carlson receive a briefing at Basa Air Base during their tour of EDCA projects on September 13. (Photo by Sgt Ambay/PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr., Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, and Admiral John Aquilino, Commander of the US Indo-Pacific Command, lauded the progress of projects under the Enhanced Defense Cooperation Agreement (EDCA) during their visit to Cagayan on September 13.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Accompanied by US Ambassador MaryKay Carlson, they inspected Lal-lo Airport and Naval Base Camilo Osias in Cagayan, as well as Basa Air Base in Pampanga, where EDCA sites are located.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/MDB2.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Admiral John Aquilino, and US Ambassador MaryKay Carlson receive a briefing at Basa Air Base during their tour of EDCA projects on September 13. (Photo by Sgt Ambay/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-14T02:11:24+08:00","hits":1017},{"id":713,"title":"PH-US delegates visit EDCA sites ahead of MDB-SEB Meeting","slug":"ph-us-delegates-visit-edca-sites-ahead-of-mdb-seb-meeting","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/277351763_332811928881224_7440173074601394112_n.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"850\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/277351763_332811928881224_7440173074601394112_n.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City –  The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), General Romeo S. Brawner Jr. together with US Ambassador to the Philippines, Her Excellency MaryKay Carlson, and Commander of the United States Indo-Pacific Command, Admiral John C. Aquilino, will visit the Enhanced Defense Cooperation Agreement (EDCA) sites in Lal-lo Airport and Naval Base Camilo Osias in Sta. Ana, Cagayan; and Basa Air Base, Pampanga, on September 13, 2023.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The leaders, accompanied by high-ranking AFP and U.S. Armed Forces officers, will conduct an extensive tour of the completed EDCA projects at Basa Air Base. The tour will also provide an opportunity for the senior military officials to gain firsthand knowledge of the bases' potential for the development of key facilities to support Humanitarian Assistance and Disaster Response (HADR) operations and modernization priorities of the AFP. </p>\r\n","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-12T03:44:11+08:00","hits":1462},{"id":714,"title":"CSAFP lauds bravery of slain CAAs, condemn use of banned APMs","slug":"csafp-lauds-bravery-of-slain-caas-condemn-use-of-banned-apms","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--General Romeo Brawner Jr, the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, lauded the selfless commitment of the five CAFGU Active Auxiliary (CAA) when he visited their wake on September 8 in Tagkawayan, Quezon.</p>\r\n<p>The five were killed by communist terrorists using banned anti-personnel mines on September 1 in the boundaries of Tagkawayan and Labo in Camarines Norte. Another soldier and two other CAAs were wounded in the incident.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/September/viber_image_2023-09-10_11-16-07-351.jpg","image_caption":"The AFP Chief, General Romeo S Brawner Jr. honors the fallen CAA members in Tagkawayan, Quezon on September 8. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-10T03:31:54+08:00","hits":1415},{"id":715,"title":" CSAFP Visits Fallen Civilian Armed Force Geographical Unit (CAFGU) Active Auxiliary Members ","slug":"csafp-visits-fallen-civilian-armed-force-geographical-unit-cafgu-active-auxiliary-members","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/CK2.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/CK2.jpg\" /><br />The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo S Brawner Jr. PA,  visits the wake and honors the fallen CAFGU Active Auxiliary Members who were killed in an encounter in Tagkawayan, Quezon. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAOAFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/CK2.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-08T08:35:23+08:00","hits":1681},{"id":716,"title":" CSAFP Visits Fallen Civillian Armed Force Geographical Unit (CAFGU) Active Auxilliary Members ","slug":"csafp-visits-fallen-civillian-armed-force-geographical-unit-cafgu-active-auxilliary-members","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/CK2.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/CK2.jpg\" /><br />The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo S Brawner Jr. PA,  visits the wake and honors the fallen CAFGU Active Auxiliary Members who were killed in an encounter in Tagkawayan, Quezon. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAOAFP)</p>","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-08T08:31:53+08:00","hits":3949},{"id":717,"title":"AFP STATEMENT | Sucessful Rore Mission in Ayungin Shoal","slug":"afp-statement-sucessful-rore-mission-in-ayungin-shoal","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"850\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Another successful rotation and reprovisioning (RoRe) mission in our post in Ayungin Shoal was completed today, September 8.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This tactical operation is a manifestation of our firm resolve to assert our sovereign rights and jurisdiction in our maritime zones, and the fulfillment of our responsibility to look after the well being of our soldiers who are stationed not only in Ayungin Shoal, but in every remote post in the country. The unprofessional act and dangerous maneuvers conducted by the China Coast Guard and its maritime militia will never prevail over our conduct of legal and legitimate operations that support rules-based international order.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">We express our deep appreciation to the guidance of the NTF-WPS and the ever reliable support of the Philippine Coast Guard in accomplishing this mission. With the strong support of our people, we will succeed.///</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-08T08:23:26+08:00","hits":2022},{"id":718,"title":"Brawner Jr hears Sweden’s pitch for AFP’s multi-role fighter project","slug":"brawner-jr-hears-sweden-s-pitch-for-afp-s-multi-role-fighter-project","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/SWE1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"636\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/SWE1.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>General Romeo Brawner Jr, the CSAFP, welcomes Her Excellency Annika Thunborg, Sweden’s Ambassador to Manila, during her courtesy visit at the AFP General Headquarters on September 8. </figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), emphasized the role of the multi-role fighter (MRF) project under the Revised AFP Modernization Program during the courtesy visit of the Sweden Ambassador Annika Thunborg to the General Headquarters on September 8. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">\"The CSAFP and Ambassador Thunborg discussed the acquisition of multi-role fighters and the recent developments in the West Philippine Sea. The ambassador likewise expressed that Sweden stands firmly behind the Philippines in the protection of its territory and territorial integrity as well as the international rules-based order and the 2016 Arbitral Award,” LtCol Enrico Gil Ileto, Chief of the AFP Public Affairs Office, said.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/SWE1.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, the CSAFP, welcomes Her Excellency Annika Thunborg, Sweden’s Ambassador to Manila, during her courtesy visit at the AFP General Headquarters on September 8. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAO, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-08T06:10:05+08:00","hits":1906},{"id":719,"title":"CSAFP to 2023 Metrobank Foundation Outstanding Filipino Soldiers: be a source of inspiration to our troops and the people","slug":"csafp-to-2023-metrobank-foundation-outstanding-filipino-soldiers-be-a-source-of-inspiration-to-our-troops-and-the-people","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/MBK2.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/MBK2.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – With their efforts towards the achievement of lasting peace and inclusive growth, the 2023 Metrobank Foundation Outstanding Filipino Soldiers (MFOFAS) were recognized by The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo S Brawner Jr. as they were presented here on September 7. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“Your stellar accomplishments in your particular domains of expertise and stations indicate your competence, zeal for duty, and fidelity in providing genuine service to the country. You shall be a source of inspiration and role models for our fellow troops and the rest of the Filipino people in striving for excellence in everything that you do,” said the CSAFP in his message that was delivered by The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, LtGen Charlton Sean M Gaerlan.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/MBK2.jpg","image_caption":"The Soldier Awardees with the Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, LtGen Charlton Sean M Gaerlan, the Executive VP of the Metrobank Foundation, Mr. Philip Francisco Dy, the Rotary Club of Makati Metro President, LtGen Raul Del Rosario, and the Chairman, TOPS, Atty. Al Miguel Leogardo.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-08T02:29:19+08:00","hits":1557},{"id":720,"title":"WESTMINCOM CHANGE OF COMMAND","slug":"westmincom-change-of-command","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/wmcm2.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/wmcm2.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Major General Steve D. Crespillo, formerly the Vice Commander of the Philippine Army, has assumed the role of Commander for the Western Mindanao Command (WestMinCom). He replaced LtGen Roy M Galido PA who is now the Army Commanding General. This transition occurred during a Change of Command Ceremony on September 5, 2023, at WestMinCom's headquarters in Camp Navarro, Zamboanga City. The ceremony was overseen by General Romeo S. Brawner Jr., Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Photos by: SSg Cesar P. Lopez</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Story by: OACPA</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/wmcm2.jpg","image_caption":"Chief of Staff Armed Forces of the Philippines Gen. Romeo S. Brawner Jr. entrusts the Command Flag to incoming WesMinCom Commander and concurrent Vice Commander, Philippine Army Maj. Gen. Steve D. Crespillo during the Change of Command Ceremony at the Headquarters Western Mindanao Command (WesMinCom), Camp Navarro, Zamboanga City on September 05, 2023.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-06T03:04:31+08:00","hits":4719},{"id":721,"title":"Philippines, United States strengthen maritime cooperation in a bilateral sail","slug":"philippines-united-states-strengthen-maritime-cooperation-in-a-bilateral-sail","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/bs3.jpg\" alt=\"Philippine Navy’s BRP Jose Rizal (FF150) and US Navy’s  USS Ralph Johnson sail through Philippine waters to carry out Division Tactics rehearsal.\" width=\"850\" height=\"478\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/bs3.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>Philippine Navy’s BRP Jose Rizal (FF150) and US Navy’s  USS Ralph Johnson sail through Philippine waters to carry out Division Tactics rehearsal.</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – As a testament to a robust maritime cooperation, the Philippines and United States are currently conducting a bilateral sail in the Philippine waters located west of Palawan.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The activity is done under the Mutual Defense Board – Security Engagement Board framework that aims to develop operational interoperability between the navies of the two countries.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/bs3.jpg","image_caption":"Philippine Navy’s BRP Jose Rizal (FF150) and US Navy’s  USS Ralph Johnson sail through Philippine waters to carry out Division Tactics rehearsal.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-04T06:09:04+08:00","hits":3061},{"id":722,"title":"CA Confirmation | CSAFP and other AFP officers","slug":"ca-confirmation-csafp-and-other-afp-officers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/br2.jpg\" alt=\"General Romeo Brawner Jr, CSAFP, and other senior military officers pose for a photo with the members of the Commission on Appointments during the deliberation their ad interim appointments on August 30.\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/br2.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>General Romeo Brawner Jr, CSAFP, and other senior military officers pose for a photo with the members of the Commission on Appointments during the deliberation their ad interim appointments on August 30.</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Thirty generals, flag officers, and senior military officers led by General Romeo Brawner Jr, the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, receive confirmation on their interim appointments and nomination from the Commission on Appointments on August 30. The list included a colonel, 25 commodores/brigadier generals, and three major generals. The confirmation of appointments made by the President is a Constitutional exercise. It also signifies the AFP’s affirmation of civilian authority over the military as enshrined in the Philippine Constitution.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/br2.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-31T01:02:46+08:00","hits":4172},{"id":723,"title":"PRESS STATEMENT | On the anniversary of the Mutual Defense Treaty","slug":"press-statement-on-the-anniversary-of-the-mutual-defense-treaty","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/TRAIN.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/TRAIN.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The MDT is one of the pillars of our national security. The mechanisms under it shall continue to be implemented to further enhance the capability of the Armed Forces of the Philippines to perform its constitutional duty of protecting our national sovereignty and territorial integrity.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/TRAIN.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-30T09:00:27+08:00","hits":2223},{"id":724,"title":"Metrobank Foundation bestows 2023 Outstanding Filipinos to Soldier-Awardees","slug":"metrobank-foundation-bestows-2023-outstanding-filipinos-to-soldier-awardees","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/MET2.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/MET2.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Soldier-awardees of the 2023 Metrobank Outstanding Filipinos from the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) were conferred with their awards as exceptional public servants in a Conferment Ceremony conducted on August 29 in Taguig City.  </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“Our aim has been to recognize those who have demonstrated exemplary leadership, integrity, and a genuine commitment to serving the people. Today’s recognition is not meant to be an endpoint. It is a call to action, a call for us to rally behind our police officers, our soldiers, our teachers, and other public officials to support their endeavors and to demand excellence from those who hold public office,” said Hon. Francis Joseph Escudero, Chairperson of the Final Board of Judges, during the ceremony. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/MET2.jpg","image_caption":"The 2023 Metrobank Foundation Outstanding Filipinos with First Lady Louise Araneta-Marcos during the Conferment Ceremony on August 29.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-30T03:11:34+08:00","hits":2231},{"id":725,"title":"AFP, Aus Defense Force Chiefs meet to showcase PH-Aus close ties; aim to conduct more exercises","slug":"afp-aus-defense-force-chiefs-meet-to-showcase-ph-aus-close-ties-aim-to-conduct-more-exercises","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/AD2 1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"641\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/AD2 1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – AFP Chief, General Romeo S Brawner Jr. welcomed the Chief of the Australian Defense Force, General Angus Campbell in a Courtesy Call here at the General Headquarters today, August 29. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In consonance with the Indo-Pacific Endeavor 2023/Exercise ALON, the two military leaders discussed the Philippines and Australia's partnership and their hopes to conduct more exercises that will help in the development of both nations' Armed Forces. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/AD2%201.jpg","image_caption":"Gen. Romeo Brawner Jr hands over a token to Gen. Angus Campbell during a Courtesy Call at the General Headquarters on August 29.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-29T07:31:32+08:00","hits":1580},{"id":726,"title":"IPE23 “ALON” closing ceremony","slug":"ipe23-alon-closing-ceremony","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/IPE3.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"523\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/IPE3.jpg\" /><br /> <br />QUEZON CITY - The Philippines-Australia (PHL-Aus) Exercise ALON 2023 closing ceremony was held at Camp General Emilio Aguinaldo in Quezon City on August 29, 2023.<br /> <br />The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP)-Australian Defence Force (ADF) bilateral amphibious training activity known as “ALON” or “waves” was conducted for the first time and forms part of Australia’s Indo-Pacific Endeavour 2023 (IPE23).</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/IPE3.jpg","image_caption":"DND Undersecretary Irineo Espino, Australian Ambassador to the Philippines Hae Kyong Yu, ADF Chief Gen Angus John Campbell, and TDCSAFP LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan pose for a photo with the planning and training staff of Indo-Pacific Endeavour-ALON 2023 during its closing ceremony on August 29 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City. (Photo by Sgt Ambay/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-29T05:32:25+08:00","hits":1403},{"id":727,"title":"National Daily, AFP collaborate for Outstanding Filipino Soldiers recognition on Heroes Day","slug":"national-daily-afp-collaborate-for-outstanding-filipino-soldiers-recognition-on-heroes-day","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/COL2.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/COL2.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – In commemoration of National Heroes Day yesterday, the Armed Forces of the Philippines in collaboration with the Manila Times, conducted a tribute to soldiers to recognize ten Outstanding Filipino soldiers for their contributions and sacrifices in pursuit of national peace and development. <br /> <br />“The partnership between the Armed Forces of the Philippines and The Manila Times for the Tribute to the Soldiers is a fitting testimony and affirmation of the importance of every soldier’s sacrifice and dedication. The story of our nation is woven from the many stories of our soldiers’ undaunted gallantry and uncommon service, all in pursuit of national peace and development,” said AFP Chief, General Romeo S Brawner Jr. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/COL2.jpg","image_caption":"Vice President Sara Z. Duterte-Carpio served as the Guest of Honor and Speaker during the Tribute to Soldiers at The Manila Hotel on August 28.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-29T03:47:21+08:00","hits":955},{"id":728,"title":"PH Navy welcomes visiting JMSDF Izumo and Samidare","slug":"ph-navy-welcomes-visiting-jmsdf-izumo-and-samidare","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/WEL.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"568\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/WEL.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The Philippine Navy extended good will to visiting Japan Maritime Self-Defense Force vessels JS Izumo (DDH-183), the lead ship of the Izumo-class multipurpose operation destroyer and JS Samidare (DD-106), a Murasame-class destroyer on August 24, 2023.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">JMSDF ships Izumo and Samidare passed close aboard of BRP Davao del Sur (LD602) in the waters off Zambales and rendered Passing Honors with their personnel Manning The Rail. LD602 responds and salutes back, with personnel aboard waving at the visiting Japanese counterparts.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Story by: NPAO</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Photos by: S1PH Dawnsri Ramiso PN / BRP Davao del Sur (LD602)</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/WEL.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-28T09:25:04+08:00","hits":449},{"id":729,"title":"NATIONAL HEROES DAY 2023","slug":"national-heroes-day-2023","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/NHD.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/NHD.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) participated in the commemoration of National Heroes Day today, August 28, at the Libingan ng mga Bayani in Fort Bonifacio, Taguig City with President Ferdinand R. Marcos Jr. as the Guest of Honor and Speaker.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Led by the AFP Chief of Staff General Romeo S Brawner Jr PA, our soldiers came together to pay tribute to our noble heroes whose steadfast dedication and selfless sacrifice have left an enduring imprint on the history of the country.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The event was highlighted by a wreath-laying ceremony, a solemn act honoring those who have devoted their lives to the service of the nation.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">(Photos by Pfc Carmelotes PN(M), PAOAFP)</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/NHD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-28T09:20:02+08:00","hits":704},{"id":730,"title":"PH-AUS EXERCISE ALON | Combined Amphibious Assault Exercise","slug":"ph-aus-exercise-alon-combined-amphibious-assault-exercise","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/camp.jpg\" width=\"960\" height=\"642\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/camp.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Philippine Navy personnel recently conducted a Combined Amphibious Assault exercise alongside the Australian Defence Force at Naval Station Leovigildo Gantioqui in Zambales on August 25.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">As part of Exercise Alon 2023 within Australia's Indo-Pacific Endeavour (IPE23) program, the simulation was aimed to practice an amphibious operation to reclaim an enemy-captured island.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Troops and amphibious assault vehicles from the Philippine Marine Corps as well as the landing dock BRP Davao del Sur LD602 were featured during the activity.</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/camp.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-28T09:13:19+08:00","hits":397},{"id":731,"title":"Philippine, Australian Armies kick off Exercise Carabaroo 2023 in Australia","slug":"philippine-australian-armies-kick-off-exercise-carabaroo-2023-in-australia","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/car.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/car.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Philippine Army (PA) and Australian Army started Exercise Carabaroo 2023 at the 1st Combat Engineer Regiment (CER) Headquarters, Robertson Barracks, Darwin, Northern Territory, Australia on August 26, 2023.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The bilateral exercise will be conducted across Gunn Point, Darwin City, Robertson Barracks, Melville Island, Tiwi Islands, and Channel Island. It aims at enhancing and increasing survivability, lethality, command, and control within the urban environment while enhancing the interoperability of multinational combined arms teams. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/car.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-27T09:08:57+08:00","hits":907},{"id":732,"title":"PH-Aus forces conduct Combined Amphibious Assault exercise in Zambales","slug":"ph-aus-forces-conduct-combined-amphibious-assault-exercise-in-zambales","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/amp.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"531\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/amp.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">SAN ANTONIO, Zambales - The Philippines-Australia (PH-Aus) Exercise Alon conducted a Combined Amphibious Assault exercise at the Naval Station Leovigildo Gantioqui on August 25, 2023.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This exercise marks the second and final phase of amphibious action after the air assault exercise in Palawan earlier this week.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/amp.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-25T09:03:27+08:00","hits":469},{"id":733,"title":"NEW SERGEANT MAJOR | FCMS Feliciano Lazo","slug":"new-sergeant-major-fcms-feliciano-lazo","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/24.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/24.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, presided over the Change of Chief of Office that installed FCMS Feliciano Lazo as the new AFP Sergeant Major on August 22 at the AFP General Headquarters.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">FCMS Lazo, who was promoted from the rank of Chief Master Sergeant during the ceremony, replaced MCPO Joe Marie Lucero who held the post in an acting capacity. FCMS Lazo comes fresh from his stint as the Command Sergeant Major of Western Mindanao Command.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP Sergeant Major is among the Personal Staff of the CSAFP, providing advice on matters concerning the enlisted personnel and non-commissioned officers of the military, including aspects of morale and discipline.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">(Photos by Sgt Ambay/PAO, AFP)</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/24.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-24T08:55:07+08:00","hits":3691},{"id":734,"title":"PH-AUS EXERCISE ALON | Static Display","slug":"ph-aus-exercise-alon-static-display","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/AL4.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"560\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/AL4.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines and Australian Defence Forces conducted a captivating static display of military assets as part of the ongoing Exercise Alon in Antonio Bautista Naval Base, Palawan.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The activity was attended by distinguished guests including Australian Ambassador to the Philippines Her Excellency, HK Yu, PSM; Chief of Joint Operations Lieutenant General Greg Bilton, AO,CSC; and Commander, WESCOM Vice Admiral Alberto Carlos.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Exercise Alon, is a bilateral amphibious training activity which includes air, maritime amphibious and follow-on land operations exercises. It aims to improve both countries’ ability to work seamlessly together, enhancing interoperability and preparedness to effectively address mutual security challenges.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">(Photos and Story by: ADF)</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/AL4.jpg","image_caption":"Royal Australian Air Force officer Squadron Leader Mark Mohr-Bell (centre) from No. 75 Squadron speaks with distinguished visitors during a static display on Exercise Alon as part of Indo-Pacific Endeavour 2023 at Antonio Bautista Naval Base, Philippines.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-23T11:47:09+08:00","hits":682},{"id":735,"title":"AFP STATEMENT | On the RoRe Mission in Ayungin","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-rore-mission-in-ayungin","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"850\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Filipinos have a reason to celebrate today. Our rotation and reprovisioning (RORE) mission was successfully conducted and the resupply boats and the PCG vessels escorting them are on their way back to their station in Palawan. Let us all pray for their safe voyage back.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP leadership commends its courageous and dedicated personnel aboard the two resupply boats who executed the operation with precision. General Romeo S Brawner Jr, the Chief of Staff, AFP expresses his deep appreciation to the assistance provided by the Philippine Coast Guard to secure the two resupply boats. He also recognizes the great efforts spearheaded by the Western Command, AFP for the proper planning, coordination and execution of the RORE mission.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-22T11:30:57+08:00","hits":1584},{"id":736,"title":"ADF’s operations chief extends invitation to Exercise Talisman Sabre","slug":"adf-s-operations-chief-extends-invitation-to-exercise-talisman-sabre","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/BIL2.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"638\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/BIL2.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--LtGen Greg Bilton, Chief of Joint Operations of the Australian Defence Forces, extended an invitation for the Armed Forces of the Philippines to participate in the Exercise Talisman Sabre in 2025 during his visit to the AFP General Headquarters on August 2022 here.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In his meeting with LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, The Deputy Chief of Staff AFP (TDCSAFP), the two discussed the possibility of the AFP joining the biennial exercise with Australia and the United States in order to achieve the common training goals with other like-minded partners in the Indo-Pacific region.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/BIL2.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, The Deputy Chief of Staff AFP, meets with LtGen Greg Bilton, Chief of Joint Operations of the Australian Defence Forces, during the latter's courtesy visit to the AFP General Headquarters on August 22.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-22T08:19:29+08:00","hits":795},{"id":737,"title":"AFP discusses its current and future vital role in the Indo-Pacific Region with US Generals","slug":"afp-discusses-its-current-and-future-vital-role-in-the-indo-pacific-region-with-us-generals","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), met with United States generals and flag officers comprising its US CAPSTONE Pacific 23-4 program and discussed about the vital role of the AFP in the Indo-Pacific Region during their courtesy visit to the AFP General Headquarters here on July 28.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“The interaction was vital in giving the delegates first-hand insights to national defense and security objectives of the AFP and its position in the promotion of a free and open Indo-Pacific region,” said LtCol Enrico Gil C Ileto, Chief of the AFP Public Affairs Office.</p>\r\n","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-22T00:40:04+08:00","hits":906},{"id":738,"title":"PH-Aus Air Assault Exercise Takes Place in Palawan  ","slug":"ph-aus-air-assault-exercise-takes-place-in-palawan","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">RIZAL, Palawan - The Philippines-Australia (PH-Aus) Exercise Alon 2023 conducted an Air Assault Exercise at Punta Baja in Rizal, Palawan on August 21, 2023.<br /> <br />This marked the first major training serial as part of the bilateral cooperation between the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the Australian Defence Force (ADF) as part of the latter’s Indo-Pacific Endeavour (IPE) activities for 2023.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/August/3.png","image_caption":"Armed Forces of the Philippines soldiers during the conduct of a bilateral air assault with Australian Army soldiers from 1st Battalion, the Royal Australian Regiment on Exercise Alon as apart of Indo Pacific Endeavour 2023 in the Philippines. (Photos and Text by ADF)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-22T00:20:26+08:00","hits":1241},{"id":739,"title":"‘Pacific Partnership’ returns to boost HADR readiness","slug":"pacific-partnership-returns-to-boost-hadr-readiness-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The annual humanitarian assistance and disaster relief (HADR) exercise, Pacific Partnership, returns to the country, in San Fernando, La Union.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Now on its 18th iteration, Pacific Partnership 2023 (PP23) is the US’ largest annual multinational HADR exercise aimed at enhancing preparedness and interoperability with seven host partner nations in the Indo-Pacific. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">From 22-31 August, PP23 will feature HADR; medical, dental, and veterinary; and engineering activities.</p>\r\n","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-21T02:18:23+08:00","hits":681},{"id":740,"title":"‘Pacific Partnership’ returns to boost HADR readiness","slug":"pacific-partnership-returns-to-boost-hadr-readiness","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The annual humanitarian assistance and disaster relief (HADR) exercise, Pacific Partnership, returns to the country, in San Fernando, La Union.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Now on its 18th iteration, Pacific Partnership 2023 (PP23) is the US’ largest annual multinational HADR exercise aimed at enhancing preparedness and interoperability with seven host partner nations in the Indo-Pacific. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">From 22-31 August, PP23 will feature HADR; medical, dental, and veterinary; and engineering activities.</p>\r\n","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-21T02:11:17+08:00","hits":773},{"id":741,"title":"PERSONNEL AIRDROP","slug":"personnel-airdrop","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/PAR4.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/PAR4.jpg\" /><br />Over 100 paratroopers from the Philippine Air Force, Philippine Army, and United States Air Force joined the military free fall mission on August 16, 2023.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><br />The free fallers and airborne qualified soldiers jumped at an altitude of 6000 ft and 1500 ft. and successfully maneuvered towards the target area in Brgy Liwayway, Sta Rosa, Nueva Ecija.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/PAR4.jpg","image_caption":"A static line paratrooper prepares for touchdown.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-17T08:50:18+08:00","hits":589},{"id":742,"title":"Low-Cost, Low-Altitude (LCLA) airdrop bundle rigging","slug":"low-cost-low-altitude-lcla-airdrop-bundle-rigging","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/AD2.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/AD2.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Philippine Air Force (PAF), United States Air Force (USAF), Royal Malaysian Air Force (Malaysia), Tentara Nasional Indonesia Angkatan Udara (TNI-AU), and Japan Air Self-Defense Force (JASDF) participated in an exchange of best practices regarding Low-Cost, Low-Altitude (LCLA) airdrop techniques on August 15, 2023, in Sta Rosa, Nueva Ecija.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">This event was part of the Flying Training Exercises within the Pacific Airlift Rally 2023. LCLA capability enables our Airlifters to quickly deliver resupply to ground operating troops and provide relief goods to areas inaccessible by land after the onslaught of calamities and disasters.</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/AD2.jpg","image_caption":"Pacific Airlift Rally | Low-Cost, Low-Altitude (LCLA) airdrop bundle rigging on August 15, 2023, in Sta Rosa, Nueva Ecija.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-17T08:43:58+08:00","hits":464},{"id":743,"title":"PH-Aus Exercise Alon 2023 Officially Kicks Off","slug":"ph-aus-exercise-alon-2023-officially-kicks-off","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/al1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/al1.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>Working together in terms of interoperability and building the Indo-Pacific region's collective capacity to respond to shared security challenges, from the left are Cmdr Barton Harrington, RAN, Commanding Officer, HMAS Anzac; Capt Brendan O’Hara, RAN, Commanding Officer, HMAS Canberra; Col Brendan Sullivan, Commanding Officer, MRF-D 23 and US Marine Corps (USMC) representative; Col Doug Pashley, CSC, Commander, Landing Forces; AIRCDRE Tony McCormack; Capt Phillipa Hay, CSC and Bar, RAN, Commander Amphibious Task Force; and LtCol Noel Gallaza PN(M)(GSC), Commander, Ph Amphibious Landing Force during the Opening Ceremony of Exercise ALON 2023. (Photos by: Sgt David Q Balisi PN(M)/Cpl Mary Joy M Hayahay PN(M)) </figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">DARWIN, Australia - The Philippines-Australia (PH-Aus) Exercise Alon 2023 officially kicked off on morning of August 14, 2023 in an opening ceremony held at the Flight Deck of HMAS Canberra with the Commander, Indo-Pacific Endeavor 2023, AIRCDRE Tony McCormack.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP)-Australian Defence Force (ADF) bilateral Cooperative Amphibious Serial conceived as “ALON” or “waves” is part of the Indo-Pacific Endeavour (IPE) activity for the year 2023. The term “waves” signifies the characteristics of amphibious warfare and emphasizes the projection of ground and air power onto a hostile or potentially hostile shore. The IPE23 is Australia’s flagship international engagement activity in the Southeast Asian and Indian Ocean region. IPE aims to promote security, stability, stronger partnership through bilateral and multilateral engagement training, capacity building and humanitarian efforts. Exercise Alon 2023 is the first bilateral amphibious exercise between Australia and the Philippines.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/al1.jpg","image_caption":"Working together in terms of interoperability and building the Indo-Pacific region's collective capacity to respond to shared security challenges, from the left are Cmdr Barton Harrington, RAN, Commanding Officer, HMAS Anzac; Capt Brendan O’Hara, RAN, Commanding Officer, HMAS Canberra; Col Brendan Sullivan, Commanding Officer, MRF-D 23 and US Marine Corps (USMC) representative; Col Doug Pashley, CSC, Commander, Landing Forces; AIRCDRE Tony McCormack; Capt Phillipa Hay, CSC and Bar, RAN, Commander Amphibious Task Force; and LtCol Noel Gallaza PN(M)(GSC), Commander, Ph Amphibious Landing Force during the Opening Ceremony of Exercise ALON 2023. (Photos by: Sgt David Q Balisi PN(M)/Cpl Mary Joy M Hayahay PN(M)) ","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-14T01:36:33+08:00","hits":3594},{"id":744,"title":"AFP Chief to Little Olympians: be our future national athletes","slug":"afp-chief-to-little-olympians-be-our-future-national-athletes","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/lo5.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/lo5.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Emphasizing the spirit of never giving up, the Armed Forces Chief encouraged the young athletes who participated in the Uniformed Services Little Olympics 2023 to compete at the national level in a Closing Ceremony conducted August 10 at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand here.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“To our participants, gawin niyo ang inyong hakbang upang madiskubre pa ang inyong talento sa larangan ng paglalaro at magbigay daan upang makaabot pa kayo sa antas tulad ng Palarong Pambansa,” Gen Romeo S. Brawner Jr., Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Chief of Staff said to the young dependents of the participating agencies of the security sector in a message that was read by LtGen Charlton Sean M Gaerlan, The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP (TDCSAFP).</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/lo5.jpg","image_caption":"Winners from the different uniformed services during the closing ceremony of the Little Olympics 2023 on August 10 at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-11T02:23:24+08:00","hits":684},{"id":745,"title":"CSAFP wants vigilance against radicalization in cyberspace","slug":"csafp-wants-vigilance-against-radicalization-in-cyberspace","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/IHL4.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/IHL4.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, called for vigilance in cyberspace to protect the youth against radicalization as he led the oath-taking ceremony in connection with the International Humanitarian Law (IHL) Month on August 7, at the AFP General Headquarters here.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">He also referenced Republic Act 11188 or the Special Protection of Children in Situations of Armed Conflict in calling for enhanced capabilities and operations in cyberspace.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/IHL4.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, CSAFP, and other officers and enlisted personnel of the General Headquarters take oath during the commemoration of the International Humanitarian Law (IHL) Month on August 7.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-07T08:05:30+08:00","hits":811},{"id":746,"title":"AFP statement on Chartered Supply Boat Blocked and Water cannoned by CCG","slug":"afp-statement-on-chartered-supply-boat-blocked-and-water-cannoned-by-ccg","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"850\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines strongly condemns and expresses grave concern over the China Coast Guard’s (CCG’s) excessive and unlawful actions against Philippine vessels near Ayungin Shoal.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-06T08:34:52+08:00","hits":697},{"id":747,"title":"Brawner Reiterates UNITY to Defenders of Southern Luzon","slug":"brawner-reiterates-unity-to-defenders-of-southern-luzon","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/SOL4.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/SOL4.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, reiterated his priorities as AFP chief to the men and women of the Southern Luzon Command that is celebrating its 36th Founding Anniversary on August 8.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">These objectives, assigned the mnemonic UNITY, covers several key points and strategies for the AFP related to Unification, Normalization, Internal Security Operations (ISO), Territorial Defense Operations (TDO), and Youth Development.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“Allow me to reiterate my priority thrusts to the team SOLCOM and deliver the principles of UNITY as we continue to enhance our troops’ warfighting proficiencies and embody a strong, reliable, and highly responsive Armed Forces,” General Brawner Jr said.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/SOL4.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, CSAFP, greets senior officers of SOLCOM when he arrived for their 36th Founding Anniversary Celebration on August 4 at their headquarters in Lucena City, Quezon Province.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-04T07:22:41+08:00","hits":2342},{"id":748,"title":"Military Educators aspire all members as Doctorate Degree holders","slug":"military-educators-aspire-all-members-as-doctorate-degree-holders","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/CP1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/CP1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Dean of the Corps of Professors of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), the AFP’s military educators, is aiming to have all of its ranks to become doctorate degree holders by 2028.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">BGen Stephen V Agtoto PROF, Dean, Corps of Professors, expressing their strong commitment to creating a culture of academic excellence, said that while everyone are masteral degree holders, only 60% of the Corps have finished doctoral programs and is aiming that everyone will have a doctorate degree by 2028. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/CP1.jpg","image_caption":"The members of the Corps of Professors, Armed Forces of the Philippines during their 82nd Founding Anniversary Celebration on August 04 at the General Headquarters.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-04T07:16:39+08:00","hits":2939},{"id":749,"title":"Soldiers, Airman named as Metrobank Outstanding Filipinos 2023","slug":"soldiers-airman-named-as-metrobank-outstanding-filipinos-2023","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/MET1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/MET1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – As public servants contributing to nation-building, two soldiers and an airman from the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) were announced as the awardees of the 2023 Metrobank Foundation Outstanding Filipinos (MFOF) in a Press Conference conducted on August 3 in Taguig City. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP awardees, together with those from the Philippine National Police and the education sector,  are SSg Danilo S Banquiao PA from the 103rd Brigade, 1ID, Philippine Army who was named as Lanao Del Sur’s Peace and Youth Empowerment Sentinel; LTC Joseph J Bitancur PAF, Assistant Commandant, Basic Military School, Air Education, Training and Doctrine Command, Philippine Air Force dubbed as Model Mentor on Military Training; and Col. Joseph Jeremias Cirilo C Dator PA, Assistant Chief of Staff for Operations (G3), Presidential Security Group, who served as an Innovator of Military Intelligence.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/MET1.jpg","image_caption":"Ten (10) Metrobank Foundation Outstanding Filipinos 2023 from the Academe, Military, and Police Sectors were officially announced as awardees on August 03.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-04T01:08:17+08:00","hits":957},{"id":750,"title":"Philippines and United States conduct joint Humanitarian and Disaster Response (HADR) Operations","slug":"philippines-and-united-states-conduct-joint-humanitarian-and-disaster-response-hadr-operations","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/lal.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"564\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/lal.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Philippines and United States conducted joint Humanitarian and Disaster Response (HADR) Operations today, August 3.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">One V-22 Osprey and two CH-53 Sea Stallions were utilized to transport 1,200 food packs and 56 solar panels to Fuga and Calayan islands to aid victims of recent typhoons.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/lal.jpg","image_caption":"Defense Secretary Gilberto Teodoro Jr and AFP Chief Staff General Romeo S Brawner Jr PA arrive in Lal-lo, Cagayan via Philippine Air Force’s Black Hawk helicopter.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-03T09:07:44+08:00","hits":743},{"id":751,"title":"Nine Ready Reserve Battalions Gear up to augment Central Luzon territorial defense","slug":"nine-ready-reserve-battalions-gear-up-to-augment-central-luzon-territorial-defense","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/7id1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/AUGUST 2023/7id1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City— Nine Ready Reserve Battalions in Central Luzon is gearing up for its transition towards territorial defense, MGen Andrew Costelo, Commander of 7th Infantry (Kaugnay) Division (7ID), Philippine Army, revealed during the anniversary rites of the 7ID held at Fort Magsaysay, Palayan City, Nueva Ecija on August 1.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In his speech during the ceremony, he laid bare his unit’s preparation for their shift of focus due to their success in counter-insurgency operations.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/AUGUST%202023/7id1.jpg","image_caption":"The 7th Infantry Division renders arrival honors to General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, during their 35th Anniversary Celebration on August 1 in Nueva Ecija.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-08-01T06:40:10+08:00","hits":1431},{"id":753,"title":"AFP STATEMENT | On Rep Castro's intent to scrutinize the proposed MUP pension","slug":"afp-statement-on-rep-castros-intent-to-scrutinize-the-proposed-mup-pension-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"850\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">We are very thankful to Representative France Castro for her concern to our retired AFP personnel and veterans. We assure her that the AFP leadership is one with her in ensuring the well-being of our soldiers after retirement.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The pension system is one way of recognizing the untiring services and selfless sacrifices of our soldiers in the performance of their duties as protector of the people and the state.///</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-07-31T14:35:36+08:00","hits":363},{"id":752,"title":"AFP STATEMENT | On Rep Castro's intent to scrutinize the proposed MUP pension","slug":"afp-statement-on-rep-castros-intent-to-scrutinize-the-proposed-mup-pension","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"850\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">We are very thankful to Representative France Castro for her concern to our retired AFP personnel and veterans. We assure her that the AFP leadership is one with her in ensuring the well-being of our soldiers after retirement.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The pension system is one way of recognizing the untiring services and selfless sacrifices of our soldiers in the performance of their duties as protector of the people and the state.///</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-07-31T14:35:36+08:00","hits":3953},{"id":754,"title":"Reserve Force as AFP's crucial asset: CSAFP lauds Reservists' contribution to National Security","slug":"reserve-force-as-afps-crucial-asset-csafp-lauds-reservists-contribution-to-national-security","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/CA1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JULY/CA1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Chief highlighted the role of the Reserve Force as the organization’s crucial asset during the first-ever National Defense College of the Philippines (NDCP) Reservists' Jamboree on July 28. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“As steadfast Filipino soldiers, may you all commit to the fulfillment of your sworn oath to the Flag and the people. This recognition welcomes you to the unparalleled world of perseverance and hard work with your co-soldiers supporting you to become an extensively knowledgeable and goal-oriented reserve force. I am sure that the AFP Reserve Command will break more barriers towards maximizing its potential as a crucial asset of the whole Armed Forces of the Philippines,” Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), General Romeo Brawner said. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/CA1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-07-28T07:27:20+08:00","hits":752},{"id":755,"title":"AFP gets closer to total victory with red headman's fall","slug":"afp-gets-closer-to-total-victory-with-red-headmans-fall","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/58B.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JULY/58B.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines is closer to its objective to immediately defeat the remaining communist terrorist group and attain total victory with the recent death of a notorious communist terrorist leader in Mindanao.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">General Romeo Brawner Jr, the Chief of Staff of the AFP, who earlier claimed strategic victory against communist and local terrorist groups, cited the military operation of the 4th Infantry Division’s on July 26 in Gingoog City, Misamis Oriental that led to the demise of communist terrorist group (CTG) identified as Dionisio Micabalo, also known as Muling, Secretary of the Northern Central Mindanao Regional Committee (NCMRC).</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/58B.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-07-28T06:53:30+08:00","hits":605},{"id":756,"title":"Brawner to Rangers: Bring Laudable Success in Countless Operations in ending Fight Against CTGs","slug":"brawner-to-rangers-bring-laudable-success-in-countless-operations-in-ending-fight-against-ctgs","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/ran1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JULY/ran1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), reiterated to the officers and enlisted personnel of the First Scout Ranger Regiment (FSRR) the order of President Ferdinand Marcos Jr to end communist armed conflict in the country this year.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In his speech as Guest of Honor and Speaker in the Change of Command Ceremony of the FSRR in Bulacan on Wednesday, July 26, the CSAFP also cited the contributions of the AFP scout rangers in strategic and tactical victories, including the defeat of high-value individuals of the communist terrorist group (CTG).</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/ran1.jpg","image_caption":"Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines and Commanding General, Philippine Army Gen. Romeo S. Brawner Jr. presents a command plaque to the outgoing First Scout Ranger Regiment Commander Maj. Gen. Freddie T. Dela Cruz during the Change of Command Ceremony at Camp Pablo Tecson, San Miguel, Bulacan, on July 26, 2023.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-07-27T03:55:02+08:00","hits":631},{"id":757,"title":"AFP Chief’s Youth Development Starts from Within Through Olympics","slug":"afp-chief-s-youth-development-starts-from-within-through-olympics","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/OL3.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JULY/OL3.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Marking the start of friendly competitions among dependents of uniformed service members, the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) hosted the Opening of the AFP-PNP-PCG-BFP-BJMP Little Olympics 2023 on July 25 at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Embodying the spirit of unity and sportsmanship, this year’s event was joined by the dependents of uniformed personnel and civilian human resources from the AFP, Philippine National Police (PNP), Philippine Coast Guard (PCG), Bureau of Fire Protection (BFP), and Bureau of Jail Management and Penology (BJMP). </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/OL3.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-07-26T00:57:33+08:00","hits":891},{"id":758,"title":"AFP Chief to Promoted Officers: Remember the Hard Work and Sacrifices of our Predecessors","slug":"afp-chief-to-promoted-officers-remember-the-hard-work-and-sacrifices-of-our-predecessors","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/D2.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JULY/D2.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), urged newly promoted generals to honor the legacy of their predecessors in a donning of ranks ceremony 9 a.m. today here. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">\"We have been bestowed the honor and responsibility to ensure that the hard work and sacrifices of our predecessors are not forgotten,\" the CSAFP said to the newly promoted officers. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/D2.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-07-25T08:56:22+08:00","hits":2022},{"id":759,"title":"AFP STATEMENT | AFP prepares vehicles for \"Libreng Sakay\" ops","slug":"afp-statement-afp-prepares-vehicles-for-libreng-sakay-ops","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"850\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">In support to the Department of Transportation (DOTr) and Metro Manila Development Authority (MMDA), the Armed Forces of the Philippines will be providing 17 military trucks, buses, and coasters from the AFP Major Services and AFP Logistics Command to assist commuters who may be affected by the transport strike on July 24 and the following days.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">This is also part of the AFP's efforts to help ensure the peaceful and orderly conduct of the President's State of the Nation Address today.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The vehicles for the Libreng Sakay will be under the operational control of the JTF-National Capital Region. They are in their respective headquarters until they are given service routes determined by the DOTr and the MMDA. The military vehicles will be deployed when called upon by the Interagency Coordinating Center.</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-07-24T12:36:33+08:00","hits":318},{"id":760,"title":"AFP CHANGE OF COMMAND AND RETIREMENT CEREMONY |","slug":"afp-change-of-command-and-retirement-ceremony","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/COC.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JULY/COC.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">General Romeo S Brawner Jr officially took the helm of the Armed Forces of the Philippines today, July 21, 2023 in a Change of Command and Retirement Ceremony in honor of General Andres Centino PA that was presided over by the President His Excellency Ferdinand R Marcos Jr. General Brawner was promoted to a four-star general and officially assumed post as the 60th Chief of Staff, AFP.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">(Photos by: Cpl Quirante)</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/COC.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-07-21T12:17:50+08:00","hits":752},{"id":761,"title":"AFP STATEMENT | On the appointment of LtGen Romeo Brawner Jr as CSAFP","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-appointment-of-ltgen-romeo-brawner-jr-as-csafp","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" width=\"1080\" height=\"1080\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines welcomes LtGen Romeo Brawner Jr as the new Chief of Staff AFP. The 145,000-strong AFP shall support the incoming CSAFP who has proven his sterling leadership and excellent performance of assigned tasks in the field of AFP operations, modernization and transformation.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">We also render our snappiest salute to our outgoing CSAFP, General Andres Centino. We wish him the best and look forward to working with him in his next position as the Presidential Adviser on the West Philippine Sea.///</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><a class=\"x1i10hfl xjbqb8w x6umtig x1b1mbwd xaqea5y xav7gou x9f619 x1ypdohk xt0psk2 xe8uvvx xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x16tdsg8 x1hl2dhg xggy1nq x1a2a7pz xt0b8zv x1qq9wsj xo1l8bm\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"link\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/hashtag/afpyoucantrust?__eep__=6&amp;__cft__[0]=AZU-_9Nd8AH4srMaWI2bu6Fe0mqnf4Y9_ebL8sPZ8XIuoIJJHMhuezmqEDCgzTbxouMQKWwefAqPq2wHWyG62FcvPPx1uzJoJzq3AwmRvtNPDk8V0yRFZfvsKmPOX55f5VlO4-KKdTbVumj7hBr7qXnZCfUauOHgbanRP7wt8XGGykrIwd3PqQUkEtm_m0mJ9k0&amp;__tn__=*NK-R\">#AFPyoucanTRUST</a></div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-07-20T20:23:40+08:00","hits":641},{"id":762,"title":"AFP launches #EveryBUDDYLabanSaHIV campaign, advocates accurate info-sharing","slug":"afp-launches-everybuddylabansahiv-campaign-advocates-accurate-info-sharing","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/H5.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JULY/H5.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Scaling up prevention services to AFP personnel, the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) launched the AFP-wide Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) Campaign called #EveryBUDDYLabanSaHIV on July 20 in Camp Victoriano K Luna, Quezon City. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Together with the Department of Defense (DOD) President’s Emergency Plan for AID Relief (PEPFAR) Philippines, the AFP-wide HIV advocates a broader understanding of HIV and encourages AFP members to collectively work on sharing correct and valuable information to reduce stigma and discrimination.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/H5.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-07-20T12:06:29+08:00","hits":611},{"id":763,"title":"AFP Educators Celebrate Six Years Capacitating Warrior Thinkers, Leaders","slug":"afp-educators-celebrate-six-years-capacitating-warrior-thinkers-leaders","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/ed.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"633\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JULY/ed.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Celebrating years of molding warrior-thinkers and leaders of the future, the Armed Forces of the Philippines Education, Training and Doctrine Command (AFPETDC) celebrated its 6th Founding Anniversary July 14 here.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Underscoring the importance of relentless and quality training for the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), the AFP Chief General Andres C Centino served as the Guest of Honor and Speaker during celebration and praised the AFPETDC for demonstrating exemplary diligence as the organization supervising the development of doctrines in the AFP. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/ed.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-07-14T15:24:10+08:00","hits":882},{"id":764,"title":"AFP honors achievements of soldier-athletes, coaches","slug":"afp-honors-achievements-of-soldier-athletes-coaches","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/CAV.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JULY/CAV.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Representing the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the country, soldier-athletes and coaches were lauded by the AFP leaders in a Recognition Ceremony conducted here on July 13.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Filled with pride, the Deputy Chief of Staff (TDCS) AFP congratulated the troops and coaches who showed excellent performance during the 32nd Southeast Asian (SEA) Games from May 05 to 16, 2023 in Phnom Penh, Cambodia. The soldier-athletes brought home 8 gold, 12 silver, and 13 bronze medals from various sports events. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/CAV.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-07-14T05:07:53+08:00","hits":924},{"id":765,"title":"PBBM emphasizes military’s professional development in line with modernization","slug":"pbbm-emphasizes-military-s-professional-development-in-line-with-modernization","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/358586087_598874315768805_5479811755447834673_n.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JULY/358586087_598874315768805_5479811755447834673_n.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The President of the Philippines and Commander-in-Chief Armed Forces of the Philippines Ferdinand R. Marcos Jr. said that the administration's commitment to AFP modernization extends beyond the acquisition of modern equipment when he addressed the 106 graduates of the Officer Candidate Course (OCC) \"GAIGMAT\" Class 58-2023 on July 7, 2023.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">During the graduation ceremony held at the Headquarters Philippine Army, Fort Bonifacio, Taguig City, the Commander-in-Chief expressed that the government is also focused on providing our soldiers with necessary skills and knowledge to excel and overcome current and pressing threats.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JULY/358586087_598874315768805_5479811755447834673_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-07-09T08:06:51+08:00","hits":777},{"id":766,"title":"AFP: Internal security gains prompt focus on territorial defense","slug":"afp-internal-security-gains-prompt-focus-on-territorial-defense","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP) General Andres Centino, said in the First Semester 2023 Command Conference that recent gains in internal security operations (ISO) will allow the military to shift its focus and resources to external defense operations.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“The AFP under the banner of our Internal Security Operations (ISO) continues with the aim of totally defeating the Communist Terrorist Group and other local terrorists. Our efforts have resulted in success with the significant reduction of their numbers and firearms and the clearing of areas where they used to maintain presence; and those countering of their, propaganda, and suppression of their financial and logistics support,” the Chief of Staff said refering to the First Semester Command Conference on July 4 here.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/July/viber_image_2023-07-04_15-08-19-990.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Chief of Staff, General Andres Centino, leads the AFP Command Conference for the 1st Semester of 2023, with senior defense officals and military officers on July 4 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City. (Photo by PO3 Viluan Ret/PAO, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-07-04T08:17:45+08:00","hits":3929},{"id":767,"title":"AFP, ADMM-Plus, meet for Final Site Survey of Medical Project","slug":"afp-admm-plus-meet-for-final-site-survey-of-medical-project","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – With the common objective to capacitate communities, the Deputy Chief of Staff for Civil-Military Operations, J7, MGen Gabriel Viray III PA met with the delegates of the ASEAN Defence Ministers' Meeting Plus Experts’ Working Group (ADMM-Plus EWG) on Military Medicine on July 03, 2023 at the AFP Headquarters. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The said meeting is for the Final Site Survey of the Project Based Community Medical Deployment (PCMD) Medical Aid Provision (MAP) which endeavors to achieve One ASEAN, One Response in addressing challenges in the region. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/July/viber_image_2023-07-04_08-24-54-020.jpg","image_caption":"The members of the ASEAN Defence Ministers' Meeting Plus Experts’ Working Group (ADMM-Plus EWG) on Military Medicine during a courtesy call today with The Deputy Chief of Staff for CMO, J7, MGen Gabriel C Viray III PA  on July 03 at the AFP Headquarters.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-07-04T08:09:59+08:00","hits":863},{"id":768,"title":"AFP Chief inspects Naval Warships in Subic","slug":"afp-chief-inspects-naval-warships-in-subic","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – General Andres C Centino PA, the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), visited three of the five naval ships docked in Subic, Zambales on Saturday, July 1 to inspect its modern warfare capabilities. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Chief of Staff boarded BRP Antonio Luna (FF-151), the Philippine Navy’s missile frigate which recently gained anti-submarine warfare capability through the arrival of the AW159 ASW \"Wildcat\" helicopter. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/July/viber_image_2023-07-02_08-31-26-206.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Chief of Staff General Andres C Centino PA poses with the officers of the Philippine Navy vessel BRP Ramon Alcaraz (PS-16).","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-07-02T15:49:31+08:00","hits":1079},{"id":769,"title":"CSAFP lauds Marines in territorial defense roles","slug":"csafp-lauds-marines-in-territorial-defense-roles","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--General Andres Centino, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), in his visit on June 30 to the northernmost military camps and detachments in North Luzon lauded the personnel of the 4th Marine Brigade (MBde) for its role in territorial defense.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The 4th MBde provides personnel to the different naval and marine detachments including the ones in Itbayat, Mavulis, Fuga, and Calayan islands tasked with maintaining territorial integrity and conducting peace and security operations, and assisting in humanitarian assistance and disaster response. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/July/IMG_0050.jpg","image_caption":"General Andres Centino, Chief of Staff of the AFP, arrives at the headquarters of the 4th Marine Brigade in Burgos, Ilocos Norte on June 30.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-07-01T15:55:50+08:00","hits":986},{"id":770,"title":"CSAFP visits troops in country’s northernmost frontier, assures support","slug":"csafp-visits-troops-in-country-s-northernmost-frontier-assures-support","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--In his ongoing philosophy of leading at the front, General Andres Centino, the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, visited troops stationed in Batanes on June 29. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The first area he visited was the Fishermen's Shelter in Mavulis Island, the country's northernmost island where a naval detachment is also located. There he led a flag-raising ceremony at a sovereignty marker.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/July/IMG_9385.jpg","image_caption":"The CSAFP, General Andres Centino, and other senior officers strike a pose at the sovereignty marker on Mavulis Island.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-30T16:00:33+08:00","hits":710},{"id":771,"title":"AFP, French Armed Forces aim to strengthen military relations","slug":"afp-french-armed-forces-aim-to-strengthen-military-relations","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Envisioning a stronger partnership between two nations, The Inspector General (TIG), Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), LtGen William N Gonzales PA welcomed the Joint Commander in the Asia-Pacific Zone of the French Armed Forces in French Polynesia, RAdm Geoffroy D' Andigné during his visit to the General Headquarters today, June 29. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">With France and the Philippines’ shared military cooperation, logistics operations, training, and education, both military leaders expressed that they look forward to further cooperation between the two nations’ Armed Forces. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/July/photo_2023-06-29_11-34-10.jpg","image_caption":"The Inspector General, AFP, LtGen William N Gonzales PA and the Joint Commander in the Asia-Pacific Zone of the French Armed Forces in French Polynesia, RAdm Geoffroy D' Andigné during his Courtesy Call on June 29 at the General Headquarters.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-29T16:05:34+08:00","hits":477},{"id":772,"title":"AFPCyG @ 5: A Game-Changer in AFP’s Mission Accomplishment","slug":"afpcyg-5-a-game-changer-in-afp-s-mission-accomplishment","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — Geared towards being a game-changer in the AFP's capabilities, the Armed Forces of the Philippines Cyber Group (AFPCyG) celebrated its 5th Founding Anniversary today, June 26 at the AFP Headquarters. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Vice Chief of Staff, AFP (VCSAFP), LtGen Arthur M Cordura PAF served as the Guest of Honor and Speaker during the anniversary celebration and said, “Cyber is the heart of our C4ISTAR [Command, Control, Communications, Computers, Intelligence, Surveillance, Targeting Acquisition and Reconnaissance]. It is a game changer. The application of cyber fundamentally changes the nature of war thereby inevitably shifting the paradigm on how we operate in a continuum of peace, conflict, crisis, and war.\"</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/June/photo_2023-06-26_15-31-41.jpg","image_caption":"The Vice Chief of Staff, AFP, LtGen Arthur M Cordura PAF served as the Guest of Honor and Speaker during the 5th Anniversary Celebration of the AFP Cyber Group on June 26, 2023 at the Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-27T01:56:13+08:00","hits":1363},{"id":773,"title":"Phil Army's ‘Men of Courage and Determination’ celebrate 61st Founding Anniversary","slug":"phil-armys-men-of-courage-and-determination-celebrate-61st-founding-anniversary","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — The Philippine Army’s Special Forces Regiment (Airborne), known for their \"courage and determination\", commemorated today in Fort Magsaysay, Nueva Ecija its 61st Founding Anniversary with the theme: \"SFRA: Competent, Resilient, and Effective SOF through the Years.\" </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP) General Andres C Centino PA joined the celebration with President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr. and the Defense Secretary, Gilbert C Teodoro Jr. in Palayan City.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/June/photo_2023-06-27_10-13-37.jpg","image_caption":"The Commander in Chief, President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr. was welcomed by the Special Forces Regiment Commander, BGen Ferdinand B Napuli PA during the 61st Founding Anniversary of SFR(A) on June 25, 2023 at Fort Magsaysay, Nueva Ecija.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-25T10:08:58+08:00","hits":1028},{"id":774,"title":"Funeral Honors for Retired General Biazon","slug":"funeral-honors-for-retired-general-biazon","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>The Armed Forces of the Philippines renders military honors to retired General Rodolfo Biazon, former AFP Chief of Staff and Senator of the Republic of the Philippines during his interment on Tuesday, June 20, at the Libingan ng mga Bayani in Taguig City in recognition of his legacy and sacrifices as a soldier, head of the military, and statesman. The service, led by the AFP Chief of Staff General Andres Centino, is the military’s way of giving its final tribute and honors in perpetuation of the memory to a dearly departed brave fellow servicemember. (Photos by A2C Castro, Sgt Ambay, and TSg Obinque/PAO, AFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/June/352805859_630662949096119_7078147268009370366_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-20T12:36:34+08:00","hits":617},{"id":775,"title":"Arrival Honors for Newly Promoted Generals and Flag Officers","slug":"arrival-honors-for-newly-promoted-generals-and-flag-officers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"https://scontent.fmnl25-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t39.30808-6/355430199_631001962395551_3386801301236615787_n.jpg?_nc_cat=102&amp;ccb=1-7&amp;_nc_sid=8bfeb9&amp;_nc_ohc=9fAxFtC_Nm4AX9q_PCI&amp;_nc_ht=scontent.fmnl25-2.fna&amp;oh=00_AfBSY1-YFwZPcddryjwcGVHjK61r_2cXIx9SgADeKDtPOQ&amp;oe=6497322B\" alt=\"May be an image of 6 people and text\" width=\"701\" height=\"467\" /></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines renders military honors to the 40 newly promoted generals and flag officers at the AFP General Headquarters on June 20. </span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Said officers were sworn to their respective duties by President Ferdinand Marcos Jr on June 19 in the Malacañan Palace, a rite signifying the supremacy of civilian authority over the military as enshrined in the Constitution.</span></p>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The ceremony was witnessed by the Executive Secretary, Secretary Lucas Bersamin; National Defense Secretary Gilbert Teodoro; the Special Assistant to the President, Secretary Anton Lagdameo; the Presidential Communications Office Secretary Cheloy Garafil; Presidential Adviser on Military and Police Affairs Secretary Roman Felix; AFP Chief of Staff General Andres Centino; and Major Service commanders. The said officers also rendered a courtesy call to the AFP Chief of Staff. (Photos by SN1 Viluan Ret/Sgt Ambay)</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/June/355430199_631001962395551_3386801301236615787_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-20T12:28:32+08:00","hits":613},{"id":776,"title":"Arrival Honors for National Defense Secretary Gilbert Teodoro Jr","slug":"arrival-honors-for-national-defense-secretary-gilbert-teodoro-jr","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">General Andres Centino, the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, leads the military in rendering arrival honors to Secretary of National Defense Gilbert \"Gibo\" Teodoro Jr in his first official visit to the AFP General Headquarters on June 19. He was welcomed by senior officers of the Joint, Personal, and Special Staff as well as enlisted and civilian personnel of Camp Aguinaldo.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Secretary Teodoro proceeded to the 12th Oversight Committee Meeting of the National Task Force on the Disbandment of Private Armed Groups with Interior and Local Government Secretary Benjamin Abalos Jr and USec Isidro Purisima of the Office of the Presidential Adviser on Peace, Reconciliation, and Unity to discuss updates on government programs to address armed violence and the problem of private armed groups. (Photos by Sgt Ambay/PAO, AFP)</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/June/viber_image_2023-06-19_15-31-35-417.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-19T12:42:52+08:00","hits":842},{"id":777,"title":"AFP supports stronger defense cooperation with Japan","slug":"afp-supports-stronger-defense-cooperation-with-japan","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/PR PHOTOS 2023/June/IMG_20230619_120822_433.jpg\" width=\"701\" height=\"700\" /></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AFP Chief of Staff General Andres Centino meets with Tsuchimoto Hideki during the latter's courtesy visit at the AFP General Headquarters on June 19. (Photo by Sgt Ambay/PAO, AFP)</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—</strong> The Armed Forces of the Philippines affirmed its support for stronger defense cooperation with Japan during the courtesy visit of Tsuchimoto Hideki, Commissioner of the Acquisition, Technology, and Logistics Agency (ATLA) of Japan on June 19 at the AFP General Headquarters here.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">General Andres Centino, the Chief of Staff AFP (CSAFP), welcomed and expressed his grateful appreciation to the Japanese official for their assistance in the AFP modernization and capability upgrade program.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/June/IMG_20230619_120822_433.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Chief of Staff General Andres Centino meets with Tsuchimoto Hideki during the latter's courtesy visit at the AFP General Headquarters on June 19. (Photo by Sgt Ambay/PAO, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-19T05:28:06+08:00","hits":744},{"id":778,"title":"AFP STATEMENT | On the death of terrorists Faharudin Hadji Benito Satar, a.k.a. Abu Zacharia and Joharie Sandab","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-death-of-terrorists-faharudin-hadji-benito-satar-a-k-a-abu-zacharia-and-joharie-sandab","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"850\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The death of Faharudin Hadji Benito Satar, a.k.a. Abu Zacharia, the so-called emir of Daesh in Southeast Asia, and Joharie Sandab, a.k.a. Morsid, DI-Philippines Sub-Leader for Finance and Logistics, in armed skirmishes today in Barangay Bangon, Marawi City has further weakened the capability of the local terrorist group to mount hostile and destructive acts. Zacharia and Morsid are facing various criminal cases in courts of law. The trust and support of our people, which resulted to successful joint law enforcement operations, motivates us to be relentless and aggressive in our counter-terrorism efforts to establish secured and peaceful communities.///</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-14T08:25:29+08:00","hits":481},{"id":779,"title":"AFP joins Nationwide Bloodletting Activity","slug":"afp-joins-nationwide-bloodletting-activity","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/viber_image_2023-06-14_18-12-58-976.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JUNE/viber_image_2023-06-14_18-12-58-976.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), in partnership with the Junior Chamber International – Manila (JCI-Manila), GMA Kapuso Foundation, Inc. (GMAKFI), and Philippine Red Cross (PRC) conducted a nationwide bloodletting activity in celebration of the World Blood Donor Day on June 14 at the AFP Headquarters.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The said activity also took place in venues nationwide with 20 sites in the National Capital Region (NCR), SM City Iloilo in Visayas, and in Davao Medical School Foundation Hospital and Lim Ket Kai Mall/Centrio Ayala in Mindanao.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/viber_image_2023-06-14_18-12-58-976.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-14T08:23:01+08:00","hits":622},{"id":780,"title":"125TH INDEPENDENCE DAY | Flag-raising and wreath-laying ceremonies","slug":"125th-independence-day-flag-raising-and-wreath-laying-ceremonies","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/viber_image_2023-06-12_15-21-01-642.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"562\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JUNE/viber_image_2023-06-12_15-21-01-642.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>General Andres Centino, the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, accompanies President Ferdinand Marcos Jr, the First Family, and Chairman Emmanuel Calairo of the National Historical Commission of the Philippines during the flag-raising and wreath-laying ceremonies at the Rizal Monument in Manila on June 12 as part of the 125th Independence Day Celebration.</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/viber_image_2023-06-12_15-21-01-642.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-12T11:12:03+08:00","hits":316},{"id":781,"title":"AFP STATEMENT | On the death of General Biazon","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-death-of-general-biazon","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/viber_image_2023-06-12_20-26-28-249.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"850\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JUNE/viber_image_2023-06-12_20-26-28-249.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines extends its sincerest condolences to the family and friends of General Rodolfo Biazon who passed away this Monday, June 12.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">General Biazon served as AFP Chief of Staff from January 24 to April 12, 1991, the first one to come from the ranks of the Philippine Marines. Prior to this, he also served as the AFP Vice Chief of Staff, Commanding General of AFP NCR Defense Command and Commandant of the Philippine Marine Corps.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/viber_image_2023-06-12_20-26-28-249.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-12T11:09:12+08:00","hits":435},{"id":782,"title":"AFP’s modern firepower to appear in 125th PH independence rites","slug":"afp-s-modern-firepower-to-appear-in-125th-ph-independence-rites","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/352663129_625315246297556_2927769077962832281_n.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"477\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JUNE/352663129_625315246297556_2927769077962832281_n.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Armed Forces of the Philippines is all set to join the 125th Independence Day Celebration tomorrow, June 12, with its modern firepower and assets joining the marquee parade as a show of enhanced territorial defense capability by the military.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Four ground-based air defense systems surface-to-air missiles, two Autonomous Truck-Mounted Howitzer System 155mm self-propelled artillery will feature in the civic-military parade, while two A-29B Super Tucano, one AH-1S Cobra attack helicopter, two Blackhawks, and two AW-109 naval helicopters will take the skies.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/352663129_625315246297556_2927769077962832281_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-11T12:30:22+08:00","hits":281},{"id":783,"title":"AFP STATEMENT | On 125th Philippine Independence Day","slug":"afp-statement-on-125th-philippine-independence-day","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"850\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Nakikiisa ang Sandatahang Lakas ng Pilipinas sa lahat ng Pilipino sa buong mundo sa pagdiriwang ng ika-125 anibersaryo ng kalayaan ng ating bansa.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Habang ating pinapahalagahan ang kalayaang ipinagkaloob sa atin ng mga bayaning nakibaka at nag-alay ng kanilang buhay, tayo ay matibay at matapang na haharap sa mga pagsubok, bitbit ang mga mahahalagang aral hango sa makulay na kasaysayan. Sa ating pinagsama-samang lakas at kaalaman, madali nating makakamtan ang hangarin para sa isang mapayapa at maunlad na pamayanan.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-11T11:06:49+08:00","hits":391},{"id":784,"title":"Empowered BARMM chiefs, cooperation with military key in peace success","slug":"empowered-barmm-chiefs-cooperation-with-military-key-in-peace-success","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/353457052_625238046305276_420449082943390829_n.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JUNE/353457052_625238046305276_420449082943390829_n.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City-–The Armed Forces of the Philippines, through the Western Mindanao Command, attributed the successful Regional Peace and Order Council (RPOC) meeting on June 10 in Maimbung, Sulu to the whole-of-nation approach as it empowered local government units (LGUs) to spearhead peace and development efforts in their provinces.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\"The meet, which for the first time was held in Sulu, was due to the cooperation of Bangsamoro Autonomous Region in Muslim Mindanao (BARMM) political and spiritual leaders' embracing their responsibility to maintain peace and security in the region,\" said LTC Enrico Gil Ileto, Chief of the Public Affairs Office, AFP.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\"The conduct of conventional and non-conventional military activities also helped significantly reduce threats and raised trust between the government and the local communities,\" he added.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The meeting was attended by various national and local leaders. It has served as a forum for thoughtful discussion and strategic planning aimed at fostering peace, stability, and progress across the region.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/353457052_625238046305276_420449082943390829_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-11T10:59:25+08:00","hits":200},{"id":785,"title":"BARMM holds historic first RPOC meeting in Sulu","slug":"barmm-holds-historic-first-rpoc-meeting-in-sulu","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/353432145_625236939638720_5798122711833597027_n.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JUNE/353432145_625236939638720_5798122711833597027_n.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Bangsamoro Autonomous Region in Muslim Mindanao (BARMM) holds its Regional Peace and Order Council (RPOC) meeting in Maimbung, Sulu today, June 10, with the different BARMM provincial officials in attendance.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The RPOC is the first to be held in Sulu and marks the significant improvements in the security situation in the area, alongside the unity of the different provincial governors of BARMM in implementing their peace and order programs.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/353432145_625236939638720_5798122711833597027_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-10T10:55:06+08:00","hits":218},{"id":786,"title":"RETIREMENT CEREMONY | BGen Calambuhay","slug":"retirement-ceremony-bgen-calambuhay","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/353035309_624595153036232_4698111095938617032_n.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JUNE/353035309_624595153036232_4698111095938617032_n.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Assistant Deputy Chief of Staff for Operations, AJ3, BGen Glenn Jun C Calambuhay PA delivers his valedictory address during the Retirement Ceremony in his honor as he officially wrapped up his active military service on June 09 at the Camp General Emilio Aguinaldo in Quezon City. The Deputy Chief of Staff for Operations, J3, MGen Fernando M Reyeg PA served as the Presiding Officer during the ceremony where he thanked BGen Calambuhay for his contributions to the Armed Forces of the Philippines. “After years of loyal service to the AFP, I am sure you feel an immense sense of pride for dedicating so much time and effort to the organization. The AFP is truly grateful for your sacrifices. Thank you for your service to our nation,” said MGen Reyeg./// <span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Photo by Pfc Carmerlotes PN(M), PAOAFP)</span></div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/353035309_624595153036232_4698111095938617032_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-10T10:51:29+08:00","hits":512},{"id":787,"title":"AFP joins 2nd Quarter National Simultaneous Earthquake Drill","slug":"afp-joins-2nd-quarter-national-simultaneous-earthquake-drill","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/EQ.jpg\" width=\"570\" height=\"855\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JUNE/EQ.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) participated in the conduct of the 2nd Quarter Nationwide Simultaneous Earthquake Drill (NSED) today, June 08 here at the General Headquarters.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AFP Officers, Enlisted Personnel, and Civilian Human Resources performed the Duck, Cover and Hold procedure at their respective units and offices. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/EQ.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-08T09:29:57+08:00","hits":450},{"id":788,"title":"Col Baclor cedes public affairs chief post to LtCol Ileto","slug":"col-baclor-cedes-public-affairs-chief-post-to-ltcol-ileto","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/CPAO.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JUNE/CPAO.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--Col Jorry Baclor, the Chief of the Public Affairs Office AFP (PAOAFP), relinquished his post to LtCol Enrico Gil Ileto in a Change of Chief of Office Ceremony on June 8 at the General Headquarters here with The Deputy Chief of Staff AFP, LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, as the presiding officer.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Col Baclor held the post since November 2021 and has since led the AFP’s public affairs campaigns in internal security operations, international defense and security engagements, humanitarian assistance and disaster response, and the AFP Transformation Roadmap and modernization program. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/CPAO.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-08T09:25:25+08:00","hits":1324},{"id":789,"title":"AFP STATEMENT | On the Appointment of new DND Secretary","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-appointment-of-new-dnd-secretary","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"850\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The AFP welcomes the appointment of Atty Gilbert Teodoro as the new Secretary of National Defense and commits its all-out support to the new leadership of the One Defense Team.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">We believe that his decisive leadership, professional competence, and wealth of experience, highlighted by his previous assignment as the defense chief from 2007 to 2009, will help build upon our gains in the defense and security of the country.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP also renders its snappiest salute to Senior Usec Carlito Galvez Jr., the outgoing DND Officer-in-Charge, for his inspiring and dedicated leadership in the Defense Department. Thank you for your service, Sir!</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-06T09:19:00+08:00","hits":231},{"id":790,"title":"PH-AUS ‘KASANGGA’ closes phase 1, phase 2 starts ","slug":"ph-aus-kasangga-closes-phase-1-phase-2-starts","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/viber_image_2023-06-06_10-37-00-492.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JUNE/viber_image_2023-06-06_10-37-00-492.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Philippine Army and the Australian Army concluded the first phase and likewise opened the second phase of the Philippine-Australia Army-to-Army Exercise “Kasangga” 23-2 at the Headquarters of 2nd Infantry “Jungle Fighter” Division at Camp Capinpin in Tanay, Rizal on June 5. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The exercise marks the AFP’s more robust international defense and security engagements with foreign military partners. Following the recent pronouncements of President Ferdinand Marcos Jr, the AFP ramped up its education and training engagements with other foreign militaries to foster trust and cooperation.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/viber_image_2023-06-06_10-37-00-492.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-06T03:02:45+08:00","hits":484},{"id":791,"title":"AFP STATEMENT | On APM explosion in Samar","slug":"afp-statement-on-apm-explosion-in-samar","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"850\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP condemns the communist terrorist group in their wanton use of banned anti-personnel mines (APM) that resulted to the death of Roel Lebico and Jerson Cabe at Barangay Magsaysay, Las Navas, Northern Samar on June 3. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">While on their way home from a hard day’s work in the construction of a farm-to-market road, the communist terrorist group detonated an APM and fired their guns on them in another case of IHL violation by the CTG.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/292899170_399126725583077_5888770797619717750_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-06T02:02:48+08:00","hits":251},{"id":792,"title":"AFP receives care packages for troops from UP Cadet Alumni Org","slug":"afp-receives-care-packages-for-troops-from-up-cadet-alumni-org","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/viber_image_2023-06-05_17-31-36-202.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JUNE/viber_image_2023-06-05_17-31-36-202.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) received care packages from the University of the Philippines Cadet Alumni Organization (UPCAO) during a Handover Ceremony conducted today, June 05, 2023 at the AFP Headquarters.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The packages were handed over by Ms. Maria Christina Cecelia Hernandez, Founder, UPCAO to MGen Gabriel C Viray III PA, Deputy Chief of Staff for Civil-Military Operations, J7. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/viber_image_2023-06-05_17-31-36-202.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-05T10:00:30+08:00","hits":253},{"id":793,"title":"AFP bares gains against communist, local terrorist groups for the month of May","slug":"afp-bares-gains-against-communist-local-terrorist-groups-for-the-month-of-may","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/viber_image_2023-06-02_14-59-53-590.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JUNE/viber_image_2023-06-02_14-59-53-590.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) continue to weaken the communist and local threat groups as 27 terrorists died, 125 surrendered, and 11 were apprehended in military operations in the month of May. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Against the Communist Terrorist Group (CTG), notable accomplishments were the successful focused military operations conducted by the 62nd Infantry Battalion in Moises Padilla, Negros Occidental and Guihulngan City, Negros Oriental on May 20 to 21, that resulted in the death of ten (10) communist terrorists and capture of 14 high-powered firearms, various ammunition, explosives, and other war materiel. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/viber_image_2023-06-02_14-59-53-590.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-06-02T07:06:01+08:00","hits":574},{"id":794,"title":"AFP holds 23rd Multi-Sector Governance Council Meeting","slug":"afp-holds-23rd-multi-sector-governance-council-meeting","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/MS.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"594\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/JUNE/MS.jpg\" /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines Multi-Sector Governance Council (AFP MSGC) conducted its 23rd Regular Meeting on May 30 at the AFP Headquarters.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The AFP MSGC Chairperson, Mr. Francisco F. Del Rosario, Jr. represented by Mr. Rex Drilon II, and the Chief of Staff, AFP (CSAFP) General Andres C Centino PA, presided over the meeting. In attendance were regular MSGC members; the Vice Chief of Staff, AFP (VCSAFP), LtGen Arthur M Cordura PAF; the Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP (TDCSAFP), LtGen Charlton Sean M Gaerlan PN(M); the AFP Joint Staff, and selected Personal and Special Staff.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/JUNE/MS.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-05-30T15:13:06+08:00","hits":631}]}